@startuml physical
' Seething Sparrows - Physical View (4+1)
' Deployment diagram: which machine runs which part of the software.

title Seething Sparrows — Physical View (Deployment Diagram)

skinparam shadowing false
left to right direction

node "Developer's PC (Windows)" <<device>> as DevPC {
  node "VS Code" <<IDE>> as VSCode
  node "Docker Desktop" <<execution environment>> {
    node "seething-sparrows container\n(python:3.14)" <<container>> as Container {
      artifact "FinalProject/ source\n(repo folder)" as Src
      artifact "FinalProject/Makefile\nflake8 / mypy / pytest / hypothesis" as Checks
      artifact "plantuml.jar + graphviz\n(make create-uml)" as Uml
    }
  }
  artifact "git + hooks" as Git
}

node "Player's PC (Windows)" <<device>> as PlayerPC {
  node "Python 3.14 venv" <<execution environment>> {
    artifact "FinalProject/src\n(main.py, objects.py)" as Game
    artifact "pygame + pymunk" as Libs
  }
  folder "FinalProject/assets/\n(sprites, background)" as Data
}

cloud "GitHub" {
  database "SeethingSparrows_OOP_Final\nrepository" as Repo
  node "GitHub Actions runner\n(ubuntu-latest)" <<execution environment>> as Runner {
    artifact "ci-test.yml\n(lint, type check, tests)" as CI
  }
}

VSCode --> Container : attaches to
Git --> Repo : push / pull (HTTPS)
Repo --> Runner : triggers CI on push / PR
Repo --> PlayerPC : git clone
Game ..> Libs : imports
Game ..> Data : loads images

note left of PlayerPC
  Usually the same laptop as the
  developer's PC. The game window
  only opens here, not in Docker.
end note

@enduml
